 127:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			/** Sends a Remote Wakeup request to the host. This signals to the host that the device should
 128:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *  be taken out of suspended mode, and communications should resume.
 129:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *
 130:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *  Typically, this is implemented so that HID devices (mice, keyboards, etc.) can wake up the
 131:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *  host computer when the host has suspended all USB devices to enter a low power state.
 132:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *
 133:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *  \note This macro should only be used if the device has indicated to the host that it
 134:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *        supports the Remote Wakeup feature in the device descriptors, and should only be
 135:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *        issued if the host is currently allowing remote wakeup events from the device (i.e.,
 136:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *        the \ref USB_Device_RemoteWakeupEnabled flag is set). When the \c NO_DEVICE_REMOTE_WAK
 137:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *        compile time option is used, this macro is unavailable.
 138:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *        \n\n
 139:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *
 140:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *  \note The USB clock must be running for this function to operate. If the stack is initialize
 141:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *        the \ref USB_OPT_MANUAL_PLL option enabled, the user must ensure that the PLL is runni
 142:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *        before attempting to call this function.
 143:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *
 144:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 *  \see \ref Group_StdDescriptors for more information on the RMWAKEUP feature and device descr
 145:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			 */
 146:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Device_AVR8.h **** 			void USB_Device_SendRemoteWakeup(void);
